        itemId = 38628,
        name = "Nether Ray Fry",
        stepCount = 10,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Complete the Skettis unlock and farm Sha'tari Skyguard Exalted before buying the pet.\n\n1. If your purchasing character is already Exalted with Sha'tari Skyguard, skip to step 10. Otherwise speak to Yuula beside Shattrath's flight master around 64.0, 42.0. Complete Threat from Above by killing 20 Gordunni ogres in the Barrier Hills north of the city, around 22.0, 12.0 on the Terokkar map. Return to Yuula, then follow To Skettis! to Adaris at Blackwind Landing, 64.0, 66.8.\n\n2. At Blackwind Landing, take World of Shadows from Severin. Kill Skettis arakkoa for 6 Shadow Dust and exchange them for Elixir of Shadows. Use the elixir to see time-lost arakkoa; keep that buff active while gathering their Time-Lost Scrolls. More Shadow Dust is repeatable, not a daily.\n\n3. Follow Secrets of the Talonpriests from Adaris with Elixir of Shadows active. Kill Zellek on the tree platform at 70.0, 74.4, Ishaal on the tree platform around 69.3, 78.5, and Skizzik in the ground-level hut at 69.8, 82.0. Loot Ishaal's Almanac and start its quest. Take it to Adaris, follow An Ally in Lower City to Rilak the Redeemed at 52.6, 20.8 in Shattrath, then return to Adaris with Countdown to Doom.\n\n4. Speak to Hazzik beside Adaris at 64.2, 66.8. Accept Hazzik's Bargain, retrieve his package from the ground-level hut in UPPER Veil Shil'ak around 74.8, 80.2, and return it. The similarly named lower village and tree platforms are not the package location.\n\n5. Accept A Shabby Disguise. Put on the supplied disguise and enter Sahaak's hut on the central island around 67.0, 79.6. Buy Adversarial Bloodlines for 3 gold and bring it to Hazzik to unlock Adversarial Blood.\n\n6. With Elixir of Shadows active, kill time-lost arakkoa until you have 40 Time-Lost Scrolls. Use a SMALL Skull Pile, such as the one around 69.6, 74.6. Spend 10 scrolls to summon each DIFFERENT descendant once: Darkscreecher Akkarai, Karrog, Gezzarak the Huntress and Vakkiz the Windrager. Loot the distinct token from each one.\n\n7. Bring the four different tokens to Hazzik. Complete Adversarial Blood for the first Time-Lost Offering; later use Tokens of the Descendants for further offerings. Accept Terokk's Downfall from Adaris, then use the LARGE Skull Pile on Terokk's Rest island at 66.2, 77.5 with an Offering in your bags to summon Terokk.\n\n8. Kill Terokk and turn in the quest. If he becomes immune, wait for the Skyguard's blue flare/fire and draw him into it to remove the shield. Repeat the four-descendant token exchange and Terokk summons; the large pile normally has about a 15-minute respawn, so collect more dust and scrolls between summons.\n\n9. Continue until Sha'tari Skyguard is Exalted. Arakkoa kills, Shadow Dust turn-ins and descendant exchanges all contribute. A simpler alternative is repeating More Shadow Dust: six dust gives 150 base reputation; 1,680 dust covers exactly Neutral to Exalted without bonuses or other gains. Dust is tradable, so you can buy only what your remaining reputation needs. You can use this alternative after step 2 instead of completing steps 3-8.\n\n10. Return to Grella at Blackwind Landing, 64.2, 66.2 in Terokkar Forest. Buy Nether Ray Fry (38628) for 32 gold at Exalted, then use the item and check the Pet Journal. The same Skyguard reputation also unlocks the five nether ray mount colors, sold separately.",
